    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d608">

                <pb facs="1353" n="1329" sameAs="frus:frus1950v03/pg1329"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">750G.00/8–850: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-08-08T14:00:00+03:00">August 8, 1950—2
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>349. British and French Embassies here having been instructed in same sense as
                        Deptel 79, July 27,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d608-f1"/> we have, on basis reasoning set forth Embtel 200, July 24,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d608-f2"/> jointly agreed to make no acknowledgment, written or
                    oral, of Soviet note on Trieste of June 20.</p>
                <p>Department pass London, Paris, Vienna, Belgrade, Rome, Trieste, USUN, Frankfort. Sent Department 349, repeated
                    info London 87, Paris 78, Vienna 10, Belgrade 12, Rome 15, Trieste 4, USUN 39, Frankfort for Reber 48.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d608-f1" n="1" xml:id="d608-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d608-f2" n="2" xml:id="d608-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; in it the Secretary of State suggested that the Embassy in the
                    Soviet Union should await the receipt by the British and French Embassies of
                    similar instructions before proceeding with the oral acknowledgment of the
                    second Soviet note. The Missions at Rome, Belgrade, and Vienna were authorized
                    to inform their respective foreign offices of U.S. views regarding the second
                    Soviet note on Trieste. (750G.00/7–2450)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
